WEBVTT

00:01:30.720 --> 00:01:34.070
The following is a work of pure fiction.

00:01:34.070 --> 00:01:37.810
<b> March 1582</b>

00:01:34.070 --> 00:01:37.810
<b>Shinano Province Takatou Castle</b>

00:02:14.640 --> 00:02:17.060
<b> Mount Fuji Skyline {ts}</b>

00:02:17.060 --> 00:02:20.870
<b>January 1582</b>

00:02:17.060 --> 00:02:20.870
<b>Kyoto Daitoku Temple</b>

00:02:31.040 --> 00:02:35.080
Caught a chill have ye, Lord Hidenaga?

00:02:35.080 --> 00:02:36.010
Nay.

00:02:36.420 --> 00:02:41.060
According to the mainland, tea was known to be the pinnacle panacea over all others.

00:02:41.690 --> 00:02:43.850
Boiled a hearty brew I have.

00:02:45.900 --> 00:02:51.400
'Twas your hands that crafted this simple red tea bowl?

00:02:51.400 --> 00:02:58.160
Indebted I was for the lovely black bowl your brother sent from Tajima.

00:02:59.760 --> 00:03:04.230
Brother is not quite as fond of black as ye, Master Senno. {until desuga}

00:03:04.230 --> 00:03:07.920
Though, the simplicity and visage of black wares intrigues me.

00:03:13.330 --> 00:03:17.100
The chill of the falling snow spreads.

00:03:23.840 --> 00:03:28.780
On the 26th day of this month, Milord had arranged to travel to Kyoto {until kyou nite}

00:03:28.780 --> 00:03:33.110
and meet with the merchant, Shimai Soushitsu.

00:03:33.430 --> 00:03:38.700
The wealthy merchant of Hakata who possesses the Narashiba tea jar?

00:03:38.700 --> 00:03:43.170
Milord yearns for the tea jar.

00:03:43.170 --> 00:03:47.220
Though Shimai Soushitsu is inconvenienced with other matters at present, {until nagaremashitaga}

00:03:47.220 --> 00:03:53.150
Milord shall request his presence once more, with the tea jar in hand.

00:03:53.590 --> 00:03:57.720
I believe Milord shall make a formal invitation after the Takeda's defeated.

00:03:57.720 --> 00:04:01.530
Aye, we also know of his residence in Kyoto.

00:04:01.530 --> 00:04:05.220
Since the meeting deals with tea, he shall request less protection.

00:04:07.350 --> 00:04:09.230
Indeed, he shall.

00:04:09.590 --> 00:04:14.230
Should General Akechi's intent to rebel ripen by then,

00:04:14.870 --> 00:04:19.200
Milord shall be slain at Honno Temple.

00:04:30.260 --> 00:04:33.860
<b> March 1582</b>

00:04:30.260 --> 00:04:33.860
<b> Shinano Province Kamisuwa {ts}</b>

00:04:33.170 --> 00:04:36.760
Alas, Osen shan't be widowed!

00:04:36.760 --> 00:04:41.410
'Twas the sturdy quality of my scale armor that spared ye!

00:04:41.410 --> 00:04:44.140
Any other ware would not have cushioned your spine!

00:04:44.530 --> 00:04:48.630
Nay General, 'twas the Holy Cross that spared my brother!

00:04:48.630 --> 00:04:52.150
Salvation lies within the teachings of God, Brother!

00:04:52.150 --> 00:04:54.610
Dare ye to attempt another such foolish venture,

00:04:54.610 --> 00:04:59.170
I, not Nishina Morinobu, shall crush your ribs!

00:05:09.330 --> 00:05:11.770
Truly, a hilarious man ye be.

00:05:12.180 --> 00:05:17.170
For attempting to bring Nishina Morinobu to surrender, you've earned my laughter!

00:05:19.190 --> 00:05:23.620
However, Nobutada has informed me of your efforts in capturing Fukuyo Castle. {until shikato kiita}

00:05:24.120 --> 00:05:29.700
For your achievements, I grant ye governance of Nishikuze Manor, worth 200 koku, {until arata ni torasu}

00:05:29.700 --> 00:05:31.770
bringing your total stipend to 400 koku.

00:05:31.770 --> 00:05:33.230
Govern these properties well.

00:05:34.690 --> 00:05:37.340
Takigawa Kazumasu, come forth!

00:05:40.820 --> 00:05:42.510
A mere 400 koku...

00:05:43.490 --> 00:05:47.270
Were my expended efforts appropriate of so paltry a reward...

00:05:47.270 --> 00:05:49.900
I would grieve, rather than remain joyous.

00:05:50.620 --> 00:05:53.710
Was the status of "Lord" beyond my grasp?

00:05:53.710 --> 00:05:56.810
Ye served and advised Nobutada well.

00:05:57.450 --> 00:06:02.720
'Twas your advice which led to the honorable deaths of Morinobu and Katsuyori. {until kiraseta}

00:06:03.220 --> 00:06:05.140
Now, the Takeda are no more.

00:06:05.610 --> 00:06:09.130
'Twas ye alone who led the successful invasion of Kai.

00:06:09.940 --> 00:06:11.860
Ye shall be rewarded.

00:06:11.860 --> 00:06:13.250
What desire ye?

00:06:19.610 --> 00:06:25.220
There is a single article I desire moreso than my own life.

00:06:25.220 --> 00:06:25.990
Continue.

00:06:26.470 --> 00:06:30.490
'Tis the Jukou Konasu tea jar that Milord possesses

00:06:30.490 --> 00:06:34.460
which I desire as my reward. {jukou konasu wo hairyou itashitaku}

00:06:43.510 --> 00:06:45.650
The Jukou Konasu tea jar?!

00:06:45.650 --> 00:06:47.510
Woe, for this envy I feel!

00:06:48.480 --> 00:06:54.670
Even Yamanoue Souji declares this to rival the Tsukumonasu tea jar!

00:06:56.030 --> 00:06:58.520
And it shall be General Takigawa's own!

00:07:14.510 --> 00:07:18.800
I award ye control of the Kozuke and Shinano provinces!

00:07:19.240 --> 00:07:21.960
Defend these territories well!

00:07:22.270 --> 00:07:25.310
I shall travel to Suruga through Kai.

00:07:25.810 --> 00:07:29.120
Should any matters of the state arise, send it in writing.

00:07:38.610 --> 00:07:42.510
R-Regardless of General Takigawa's accomplishments,

00:07:42.510 --> 00:07:44.990
even he was denied the tea jar?!

00:07:51.160 --> 00:07:53.950
Forgive me for taking the risk of sending this letter.

00:07:54.500 --> 00:07:55.770
General Akechi...

00:07:57.080 --> 00:08:00.910
I write to ye in my most arduous of hours.

00:08:02.840 --> 00:08:07.990
Milord intends to forgo granting ye control of Shikoku Islands {until kutsugaeshi}

00:08:08.690 --> 00:08:13.900
as Milord shall allow Miyoshi Yasunaga of Kawachi the Awa Province on the island. {until atai ni naru to iu}

00:08:15.210 --> 00:08:21.720
General, ye devoted many years to conquering those isles.

00:08:22.940 --> 00:08:28.930
Milord's decision to revoke your right to the isles be ill-advised.

00:08:30.250 --> 00:08:35.640
Though ye, General, have many devoted warriors within your clan,

00:08:36.060 --> 00:08:42.470
Milord ignores your achievements, and deems to rule absolute alongside his kin. {until shiteorareru}

00:08:43.660 --> 00:08:47.830
We vassals and Lords exist so long as we conquer his foes.

00:08:50.210 --> 00:08:56.860
Otherwise, I fear we may be disposed after achieving unification.

00:09:02.970 --> 00:09:08.380
'O kind General, were ye to share my concern for our clans,

00:09:09.710 --> 00:09:15.820
perhaps ye may depose Milord from his throne.

00:09:24.450 --> 00:09:26.080
I...

00:09:29.500 --> 00:09:33.200
must inquire this of Milord.

00:09:40.300 --> 00:09:41.600
General Takigawa.

00:09:42.480 --> 00:09:45.850
You have my condolences for the earlier affair.

00:09:46.780 --> 00:09:53.010
Had I commanded our forces to victory, I would have requested the very tea jar.

00:09:53.640 --> 00:09:59.080
The Jukou Konasu tea jar is a grand treasure, befitting of an Emperor.

00:09:59.080 --> 00:10:02.000
'Twas naught of haught to have asked for such a reward.

00:10:02.000 --> 00:10:06.460
Though, permission to Milord's tea ceremonies would have sufficed.

00:10:06.850 --> 00:10:10.350
However, there is little to despair over.

00:10:10.350 --> 00:10:15.450
Now, ye administrate the entirety of the Kantou region.

00:10:15.450 --> 00:10:20.490
Were war to come, expenditures would come not from your clan, but from Kantou.

00:10:21.080 --> 00:10:23.020
Spare me your words of comfort.

00:10:23.310 --> 00:10:26.580
Kozuke is a barren land without beauty.

00:10:27.030 --> 00:10:33.050
Woe, for the Uesugi and Hojo remnants lie on the borders of Kozuke.

00:10:33.450 --> 00:10:35.540
Though I am but a modest aesthete, {until hashikure}

00:10:35.540 --> 00:10:39.260
sending me away from Kyoto is akin to death.

00:10:39.900 --> 00:10:43.870
Does Milord desire my death to tigers?

00:10:43.890 --> 00:10:49.040
Perhaps, vassals not of Milord's kin shan't ever ascend him.

00:10:49.950 --> 00:10:55.050
"To hares, hounds; to hounds, Death."

00:10:55.050 --> 00:10:57.380
'Tis a proverb of the Tang Dynasty. {until kourousha mo}

00:10:57.380 --> 00:11:01.060
Servants are discarded once they've outlived their purpose to their Lord.

00:11:01.060 --> 00:11:06.430
Myself, General Akechi, and General Hashiba are not of Milord's kin.

00:11:06.430 --> 00:11:11.090
To Milord, I shan't become naught but a hound...

00:11:12.260 --> 00:11:17.330
My clan's allegiance and loyalty remains toward Milord's clan.

00:11:18.450 --> 00:11:22.100
However, denied I would be for any further feats...

00:11:24.060 --> 00:11:26.730
I've not been struck by lightning!

00:11:26.730 --> 00:11:28.630
I shall continue my ascent!

00:12:05.460 --> 00:12:06.400
Nay.

00:12:07.080 --> 00:12:08.370
I shan't...

00:12:09.300 --> 00:12:13.010
My loyalty to Milord shan't waver!

00:12:43.010 --> 00:12:45.410
I've already appointed the administrator of Shikoku.

00:12:46.390 --> 00:12:47.910
I was not aware.

00:12:48.440 --> 00:12:50.940
My son, Nobutaka, shall serve as administrator.

00:12:52.590 --> 00:12:56.990
Withdraw your forces from the isles, and I shall award ye control {until kawari ni}

00:12:56.990 --> 00:12:59.120
over the Iwami and Izumo provinces.

00:13:00.480 --> 00:13:05.130
Territories of mountain and barren rock shan't compensate for my clan's efforts!

00:13:05.130 --> 00:13:08.680
Do ye desire my clan to perish?!

00:13:13.070 --> 00:13:20.150
Know that I shall unearth and seize all within this nation!

00:13:21.360 --> 00:13:25.540
'Tis my first trial to becoming "Emperor!"

00:13:33.590 --> 00:13:35.380
Behold, Mitsuhide.

00:13:40.470 --> 00:13:42.330
The refreshing beauty of Mount Fuji.

00:13:43.280 --> 00:13:48.530
The jewel of the Takeda clan is now my own!

00:13:49.250 --> 00:13:54.660
Perhaps the Ming Mainland and the barbarians possess such riches.

00:13:55.770 --> 00:13:59.260
Nevertheless, I shall seize them as well!

00:14:15.410 --> 00:14:18.980
<b> April 1582</b>

00:14:15.410 --> 00:14:18.980
<b> Bicchu Province Takamatsu</b>

00:14:15.410 --> 00:14:18.980
<b> Hashiba Hideyoshi's Main Camp {ts}</b>

00:14:26.810 --> 00:14:28.050
General Hashiba,

00:14:28.050 --> 00:14:32.350
Generals Kuroda Yoshitaka and Hachisuka Masakatsu have arrived.

00:14:32.950 --> 00:14:33.810
I shall see them.

00:14:33.810 --> 00:14:34.940
Aye.

00:14:37.080 --> 00:14:38.800
Show no concern!

00:14:40.370 --> 00:14:41.690
F-Forgive me, Milord.

00:14:45.880 --> 00:14:50.220
The Mori clan's grasp over the Chugoku region has weakened significantly.

00:14:50.220 --> 00:14:52.910
Regardless of Takamatsu Castle's fortifications and mountainous terrain,

00:14:52.910 --> 00:14:57.710
General Shimizu Muneharu holds it with a mere 5,000 men.

00:14:57.710 --> 00:15:00.340
Our forces number 25,000.

00:15:00.620 --> 00:15:05.590
Grant me command, and I shall capture Takamatsu Castle without a single casualty.

00:15:05.890 --> 00:15:07.590
And what of Mori Terumoto's stance?

00:15:07.830 --> 00:15:13.600
The messengers he sends for negotiations ask for naught but peace.

00:15:14.120 --> 00:15:17.010
Mori Terumoto welcomes peace moreso than any.

00:15:17.010 --> 00:15:19.000
The garrison at Takamatsu Castle is naught but a show.

00:15:19.000 --> 00:15:22.030
Perhaps he intends the castle as an offering.

00:15:22.610 --> 00:15:25.040
Grant me command, Milord.

00:15:25.040 --> 00:15:27.550
Haste is unnecessary at this junction.

00:15:28.460 --> 00:15:32.520
Chugoku tends to experience frequent floods.

00:15:33.070 --> 00:15:35.280
Hither, shall the rains fall. {mamonaku tsuyu ni hairu}

00:15:35.930 --> 00:15:41.570
Damming and unleashing the waters of the Kawazugahana river shall serve to flood Takamatsu Castle.

00:15:41.570 --> 00:15:47.630
'Twill be then, when we may capture Takamatsu Castle without a single casualty.

00:15:51.680 --> 00:15:52.880
Aye.

00:15:56.240 --> 00:15:58.350
Has there been any word from General Akechi?

00:15:58.350 --> 00:15:59.850
Not a word has arrived, Brother.

00:16:01.560 --> 00:16:07.200
'Twas I who recommended Miyoshi Yasunaga to Milord for Awa,

00:16:08.030 --> 00:16:10.820
yet Akechi clings to hesitation!

00:16:10.820 --> 00:16:14.470
Master Senno frequently visits General Akechi.

00:16:14.890 --> 00:16:20.830
For crushing the Takeda clan, the Emperor shall award Milord a position within the Imperial Court.

00:16:20.830 --> 00:16:23.340
Milord is to be appointed early into the sixth month {until awase} during a tea ceremony in Kyoto,

00:16:23.340 --> 00:16:29.190
where Shimai Soushitsu shall be present, with the Narashiba tea jar in hand. {until jyouraku suru de arouto}

00:16:29.840 --> 00:16:32.850
Only a single month remains.

00:16:33.500 --> 00:16:37.370
Generals alike Kuroda and Hachisuka treat my actions with suspicion.

00:16:37.960 --> 00:16:41.040
Should I bide any further, their morale shall dwindle.

00:16:41.590 --> 00:16:45.350
I intend to request Milord for reinforcements, to calm their suspicions.

00:16:45.350 --> 00:16:49.690
You shall request General Akechi, who shall pass through Honno Temple?

00:16:50.100 --> 00:16:53.370
Should he fail our expectations, what then?

00:16:57.000 --> 00:16:59.930
Master Soueki shall take responsibility as our instigator.

00:17:01.550 --> 00:17:05.300
<b> May 1582</b>

00:17:01.550 --> 00:17:05.300
<b> Omi Province Azuchi Castle</b>

00:17:01.550 --> 00:17:05.300
<b> Akechi Mitsuhide's Residence {ts}</b>

00:17:12.140 --> 00:17:16.420
At last, I behold the Hakkaku tea kettle bestowed by Milord!

00:17:17.600 --> 00:17:20.630
'Tis a masterpiece which unites the rough visage of a warrior

00:17:20.630 --> 00:17:24.060
as well as the worn polish of an aged vessel.

00:17:24.440 --> 00:17:27.080
At last, I've consumed its visage!

00:17:30.590 --> 00:17:33.950
Elegant, yet poetic is this scroll.

00:17:33.950 --> 00:17:37.450
'Twas by the very hand of Milord.

00:17:41.280 --> 00:17:44.160
Ye must be aware by now, I am certain.

00:17:44.160 --> 00:17:48.180
General Tokugawa Ieyasu shall attend a banquet at Azuchi Castle in celebration

00:17:48.180 --> 00:17:49.950
of our victory over the Takeda clan. {until azuchi he mairaremasu}

00:17:50.360 --> 00:17:54.650
Milord has ordered me to oversee the food to be served.

00:17:55.140 --> 00:17:57.970
'Tis an occasion in which failure must remain absent.

00:18:00.370 --> 00:18:04.240
Might ye alleviate my qualm?

00:18:04.240 --> 00:18:06.580
Very well. {watakushi de yokereba}

00:18:06.580 --> 00:18:11.120
I shall provide ye with the finest ingredients from the port of Sakai.

00:18:11.520 --> 00:18:12.610
However...

00:18:13.490 --> 00:18:16.720
I, alone, may be deemed insufficient.

00:18:17.780 --> 00:18:21.640
Ye suggest another join in your company?

00:18:21.640 --> 00:18:24.790
Aye, and he should prove most reliable.

00:18:25.260 --> 00:18:26.830
Me...?

00:18:26.830 --> 00:18:33.300
My disciple, Yamanoue Souji, shall serve and assist as I shall.

00:18:33.650 --> 00:18:34.530
Curses... {gaku}

00:18:34.530 --> 00:18:35.780
Though...

00:18:35.780 --> 00:18:41.940
I doubt Souji shall be rival General Tokugawa in terms of company.

00:18:41.940 --> 00:18:48.820
Perhaps a certain man, refined in both art and war, may suffice... {until yoi no desu ga}

00:18:58.430 --> 00:19:03.100
I would have Governor Furuta serve as my second assistant.

00:19:03.470 --> 00:19:05.890
Do ye acquiesce, Governor Furuta?

00:19:10.830 --> 00:19:14.850
I gratefully accept this grand honor.

00:19:15.890 --> 00:19:19.850
I shall assist in ensuring the banquet a grand success.

00:19:21.870 --> 00:19:25.150
Though I am denied a seat at Milord's tea ceremonies,

00:19:25.150 --> 00:19:28.890
I may display my finesse and aesthetics at a banquet!

00:19:29.550 --> 00:19:31.240
Very well!

00:19:31.240 --> 00:19:34.650
Fame shall be showered unto my clan!

00:19:41.740 --> 00:19:44.800
Master Senno.

00:19:44.800 --> 00:19:49.540
If memory serves, your tea brewery is known as "simple brewery," aye?

00:19:49.540 --> 00:19:54.550
I've yet to grasp the concept of simplicity's role with the complexity of tea. {from watakushi ni wa until wakarimasenu}

00:19:56.550 --> 00:20:03.060
I've pondered naught but of aesthetics as of late.

00:20:07.040 --> 00:20:13.070
General, aware ye may be that I am ripened moreso than yourself.

00:20:13.470 --> 00:20:22.330
Hither, should ye travel into the presence of Death, and only then shall ye accept the role of simplicity.

00:20:32.050 --> 00:20:35.460
Alas, I've grasped the mind of General Akechi.

00:20:36.420 --> 00:20:40.180
I have a tendency to judge others based on possessions.

00:20:40.580 --> 00:20:45.490
Now that I've beheld both treasures of General Akechi...

00:20:45.850 --> 00:20:52.020
aware I am of the piety both he and General Hashiba share towards Milord.

00:20:55.460 --> 00:20:56.890
Do pardon my tact.

00:20:56.890 --> 00:21:00.490
I desired naught but to share my ingenuity.

00:21:01.070 --> 00:21:03.490
Farewell, Master Soueki.

00:21:07.330 --> 00:21:09.660
Naïve, is the young governor.

00:21:11.650 --> 00:21:17.560
The Hakkaku tea pot is meant not to be used above, but in the hearth below.

00:21:19.900 --> 00:21:26.260
Doubtless is the general of this, and yet he displayed both pot and scroll.

00:21:26.640 --> 00:21:32.280
He had done so to conceal his forsaken loyalty to Milord,

00:21:32.280 --> 00:21:35.120
and displayed was his displeasure.

00:21:37.230 --> 00:21:40.280
Also, his lust for simplicity.

00:21:40.660 --> 00:21:43.950
In great despair, is General Akechi.

00:21:43.950 --> 00:21:47.850
Aye, have the seeds of rebellion sprout buds from within.

00:22:07.890 --> 00:22:09.330
May this...

00:22:10.410 --> 00:22:15.900
object of countless teeth, akin to ogre fangs, be considered food?

00:22:16.470 --> 00:22:19.470
I've not beheld such food either,

00:22:19.470 --> 00:22:26.430
for the port of Sakai imports exotic articles from Luzon, Ryukyu, and the Barbarians.

00:22:36.570 --> 00:22:39.640
'Twould be best to avoid the puddles.

00:22:39.640 --> 00:22:44.230
The folk of Azuchi would make merry at our muddied steeds.

00:22:44.230 --> 00:22:45.440
Let them make merry.

00:22:46.070 --> 00:22:49.160
A traveled steed is all but pristine.

00:22:49.760 --> 00:22:52.140
Should any dare to ridicule our visages...

00:22:52.650 --> 00:22:55.370
they would not be true warriors.

00:24:36.060 --> 00:24:37.700
<b> 'Tis most proper of a true warrior</b>

00:24:43.230 --> 00:24:44.870
<b> Behold, "Mount Azuchi!" {ts}</b>

00:24:48.240 --> 00:24:49.870
<b> Protest, do ye? {ts}</b>

00:24:49.870 --> 00:24:52.680
Dining in Hell.

00:24:53.090 --> 00:24:57.960
Does the fork joining the aesthete and warrior exist?

00:24:56.640 --> 00:24:59.960
<b> Dining in Hell</b>
